Check the teardown pin on this machine: that it can be read, and that the stored
binary for this platform exists and still has the sha256 the pin records. Exit 0
means removal would run: the pin is intact, or there is none and this is a
release build, which needs none. A development build with no pin, or any other
problem, is reported on stderr with exit 1. The text report ends with a line
saying what `worktree remove` would do, which also takes into account where the
control home is and who can write it. With --json, one document on stdout whose
"removal" is "pin", "this-build" or "refuse"; with no pin, {"pinned": false,
"removal": …}; empty stdout with exit 1 means the pin could not be read.

Usage:
  treerig teardown status [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for status
      --json   machine-readable output

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
